  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING CHANGES (11.0.0):\n            - services.AddAssertableHttpClient(configuration, s => ...) is the only public registration; it is all you call.\n              The started host's provider is handed to the asserts automatically.\n            - Removed from the public API: HttpClientAssertExtensions.Setup(provider), HttpClientAssertExtensions.Setup(s => ...),\n              services.AddTestSdkSettings, AddAssertableHttpClientFactory, the consumerAssembly parameter, and every other\n              services.Add...() building block with the service interfaces behind it.\n\n            NEW FEATURES:\n            - Own error handlers: ITestErrorHandler / TestErrorHandler<TException> are public and asked before the catch-all.\n\n            FIXES:\n            - A response body carrying its own content.value is no longer mistaken for the snapshot envelope.\n\n            Full details: RELEASE-NOTES.md in the repository.",
